  "worksAsStation": false,
  "description": "Mark four lanes that run the length of the ice. Each skater starts in a corner with a puck, goes down lane 1, back up lane 2, down lane 3 and back up lane 4, with a different puck skill in each lane. The next skater goes when the one ahead is halfway down lane 1.",
  "steps": [
    "Lane 1, down: narrow-wide, close to you then far out.",
    "Lane 2, back: toe drags, in front and to the side.",
    "Lane 3, down: drop the puck to your skates, kick it back to your stick.",
    "Lane 4, back: your own best moves."
  ],
